<title>FRANCE: AGF 1996 profit rises 42 percent.</title>
<headline>AGF 1996 profit rises 42 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net consolidated profit		  1,536  vs	 1,082</p>
<p>    Life insurance France			376  vs	   222</p>
<p>    Non-life insurance France		  937  vs	   404</p>
<p>    Insurance outside France		   817  vs	   924</p>
<p>    Credit insurance			     341  vs	   268</p>
<p>    Insurance activities		     2,471  vs	 1,818</p>
<p>    Reinsurance				    175  vs	   166</p>
<p>    Banking				 loss   526  vs   loss  490</p>
<p>    Holdings and property companies	   45  vs	    13</p>
<p>    Net pre-exceptional before goodwill  2,165  vs	 1,507</p>
<p>    Amortisation of goodwill	loss     424  vs   loss  410</p>
<p>    Net pre-exceptional after goodwill   1,741  vs	 1,097</p>
<p>Exceptionals</p>
<p>    - Income					 nil  vs	 2,557</p>
<p>    - charges			     loss   205  vs  loss 2,572</p>
<p>NOTE - Assurances Generales de France (AGF) gave the results in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
